summary:
Short answer: the data layer today is a cache, not a knowledge base. The S80 data_supply digest still holds at 95cf6f86. Images and identity are still never stored, and the L2 price read still drops fetched_at.

L1 (Redis) keys are md5 hashes of brand|name|variant:
- specs:<h12> for 7 days.
- price:<h12> sized by build_size_aware_price_cache_key: 7 days for a genuine Bahrain price, 24 h for converted or estimated.
- nogenuine:<price key> for 30 days (24 h when transient).
- reviews:<h12> for 7 days.

L2 is three migration-012 tables. Their product_key is that same prefixed L1 string, so specs, price and reviews rows for one product never share an id:
- product_specs: upsert, 30-day window.
- product_prices: append-only, 7-day / 24-hour windows, no retention.
- product_reviews: upsert, 14-day window.

On a full cache hit a compare still pays three things: the parse LLM, the gpt-4o verdict, and a fresh image lookup (paid Serper Images or GPT, because the unified search is skipped). The unified-search gate checks L1 only, so a product that misses L1 but hits L2 still buys a Serper search.

Never persisted today:
- images;
- identity resolution (parse and vision output);
- per-host health beyond provider circuit breakers and 30-day hit counters;
- citation snippets (attached after the cache write);
- robots state (only a 2026-08-31 robots_allowed snapshot in search_descriptors.json; the live price path runs no robots check);
- the feedback-to-product join;
- the `products` table (its upsert has zero callers).

Comparisons are saved only for signed-in users.

The registry is two parts merged once, at import:
- 40 literal Source rows;
- data/bh_gcc_sources.json: 368 rows, of which 275 are live, 61 dead, 18 provider-test-candidate and 14 render-only; 95 carry a search descriptor.

The loader drops the country and genuine_method fields. Because the merge happens at import, ENABLE_BH_GCC_CATALOG_SOURCES needs a restart, unlike the per-call flags. Host matching is first-suffix-wins unless ENABLE_LONGEST_HOST_MATCH is on.

Supabase:
- The 012 policies are USING(true) for every role, so the public anon key can read, insert and update the product tables (repo SQL; the live database is not verified). That is a poisoning risk for an owned knowledge base.
- New tables should follow the 032/035/044 pattern: RLS on, service-role-only.
- The next free migration number is 045 (035 and 036 are unapplied, 039 is reserved, 044 is applied).
- Writes go through get_admin_supabase_client plus run_db, fire-and-forget.

Building a knowledge base that grows with every request needs:
- one canonical product id (derived from the existing identity token) instead of three prefixed hashes;
- variants as a separate entity;
- offers per merchant with captured_at, stock and URL;
- an image table;
- specs with citations;
- reviews with source and provenance;
- a merchant table holding platform, adapter, health, robots state and last crawl;
- one write point after build_comparison_response that runs for every compare, not only signed-in ones.
